# Alderwick & Rowe — AI-Powered Real Estate Platform

**An AI-assisted property enquiry and client engagement system built as an independent real estate automation case study.**

[🌐 Explore Live Website](https://stellar-seahorse-7ca03c.netlify.app/) | [💻 View Source Code](https://github.com/johnbangs/Alderwick-Rowe)

**Developer:** Abass John Bangura  
**Specialisation:** AI Automation Engineering | AI Agents | Workflow Integration  
**Project Type:** Independent Simulated Business Case Study

---

## 1. Project Overview

Alderwick & Rowe is a simulated UK estate agency platform designed to explore how modern web applications, AI-assisted customer engagement, and automated workflows can work together.

The project combines a responsive property website with structured enquiry intake, a client advisory chat interface, and integration capabilities for n8n.

The objective is to demonstrate a practical approach to connecting customer-facing digital experiences with intelligent business processes.

## 2. The Business Problem

Property businesses often manage enquiries from multiple channels. Manual handling can introduce several operational challenges:

- Delays in responding to prospective customers.
- Repetitive collection of client and property requirements.
- Inconsistent enquiry information.
- Disconnected communication between websites and internal workflows.
- Difficulty maintaining a structured record of incoming enquiries.

## 3. The Proposed Solution

The platform provides a central digital experience for property discovery and enquiry submission.

Its architecture is designed to support:

- Structured property enquiry capture.
- AI-assisted client interaction through an advisory chat interface.
- Enquiry transmission to an n8n webhook.
- Resilient submission handling and client-side recovery for network failures.
- Property information and document access.
- Responsive website navigation across devices.

## 4. Technical Architecture

The application follows a website-to-automation integration approach:

**Visitor → React Website → Enquiry Form / Advisory Chat → Webhook Integration → n8n Automation Workflow**

Key technical components include:

**Frontend:** React, TypeScript, Vite and Tailwind CSS.

**AI integration:** Google GenAI dependency and an AI-assisted customer interaction experience.

**Automation:** n8n and webhook-based enquiry integration.

**Supporting technologies:** Express, Zod, GitHub and Netlify.

## 5. Implemented Features

The repository's launch checklist documents the following capabilities:

**Enquiry Management**
- Structured submission payload containing 18 defined enquiry fields.
- Submission confirmation and failure-handling flows.
- Local queuing for failed or offline enquiries.
- Client-side spam-reduction measures.

**Customer Interaction**
- Advisory chat interface.
- Property-related context and contact capture.
- Integration of enquiry interactions with the automation intake process.

**Property Experience**
- Structured property listing data.
- Property-specific information and downloadable documents.
- Responsive client-facing website.

**Engineering & Website Quality**
- SEO metadata and structured data.
- Cookie consent and legal-information pages.
- Accessibility-focused form and navigation features.
- Developer diagnostics for webhook payload testing.

These features are documented in the project repository. Production readiness and end-to-end integration should be validated separately.

